      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt from \u0027\u003Ci\u003EPot-luck; or, The British home cookery book\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by May Byron (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#byron-1914\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EByron 1914\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "343. SAVOURY PUDDING (Sussex)\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nHalf a pound of stale bread, three eggs, three ounces of flour, three ounces of suet, one ounce of fine oatmeal, one pint of mUk, a small shalot chopped very fine, a little salt, a pinch of sweet marjoram, and enough lemon to give a fiavour. Mix all thoroughly well together, not too moist: turn into a basin or (better) a floured cloth, and boil or steam for three hours.\u003Cbr\u003E"
